TESTFILE33

Scratch file for the two-machine claim test. Nothing reads it.

macbook waited for bdrm's claim on this path to clear before writing:

  bdrm claimed TESTFILE33          conflict warning fired on check
  bdrm released ~40s later         "holding nothing — released"
  macbook claimed it, wrote this

That is the whole handoff, and it is the first one that has run between two
machines without either side coordinating out of band.

Second run, 2026-08-03, both machines on v0.2.0 against the migrated relay:

  bdrm claimed TESTFILE33          conflict fired, "claimed 7s ago"
  macbook polled in the background rather than sitting idle
  bdrm went quiet holding it       "claimed 2m ago (idle 2m)"
  bdrm released explicitly         "released — working on ..."
  macbook claimed it, wrote this

Two things showed up here that the first run could not:

The idle indicator distinguished "still editing" from "stopped, still
holding" — bdrm's claim froze at 2m while the file stayed locked. Under the
old display both looked identical, and you had to watch the number across
two checks to tell.

Claim history crossed machines. bdrm's previous plan rendered as (previous)
underneath its live one, which means claimed_at and the append-only plan
rows survive the wire between two hosts, not just two processes on one.
